# Ownership is what replaces the repo boundary you lose by merging repos.
#
# Rules are last-match-wins, so order matters: the broad platform rules come
# first and the specific per-service rules override them.
#
# The teams below must exist under the AlgoGators org before GitHub will honour
# these lines — an unresolvable team is silently ignored, which looks exactly
# like working ownership until someone merges without review. Verify with:
#     gh api /repos/AlgoGators/algogators/codeowners/errors

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: nothing is unowned.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @AlgoGators/platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI machinery. The reusable workflows and the path linter are load-bearing for
# every service, so they stay with platform even though service teams own the
# callers that invoke them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/_*.yml           @AlgoGators/platform
/.github/workflows/security.yml     @AlgoGators/platform
/.github/workflows/meta-*.yml       @AlgoGators/platform
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @AlgoGators/platform
/platform/ci/                       @AlgoGators/platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared definitions. A contract change breaks producers and consumers at once,
# so it needs review from the people on both sides of it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/platform/contracts/                @AlgoGators/platform @AlgoGators/data @AlgoGators/execution
/platform/configs/                  @AlgoGators/platform @AlgoGators/execution

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Toolchain roots. Changing these changes every member's build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/pyproject.toml                     @AlgoGators/platform
/uv.lock                            @AlgoGators/platform
/pnpm-workspace.yaml                @AlgoGators/platform
/CMakePresets.json                  @AlgoGators/platform
/vcpkg.json                         @AlgoGators/platform
/justfile                           @AlgoGators/platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-service. Each team owns its directory AND the workflow files that gate it,
# so a service can tune its own coverage floor without a platform review — but
# cannot edit the reusable everyone else depends on.
#
# Uncomment each block as the service is migrated in.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/libs/algosystem/                    @AlgoGators/research
/.github/workflows/lib-algosystem.*  @AlgoGators/research
/libs/research-core/                 @AlgoGators/research
/.github/workflows/lib-research-core.* @AlgoGators/research

/services/data-ngin/                 @AlgoGators/data
/.github/workflows/svc-data-ngin.*   @AlgoGators/data

/services/trade-ngin/                @AlgoGators/execution
/.github/workflows/svc-trade-ngin.*  @AlgoGators/execution
/services/research-api/              @AlgoGators/research
/.github/workflows/svc-research-api.* @AlgoGators/research

/apps/algolens-web/                  @AlgoGators/frontend
/.github/workflows/app-algolens-*    @AlgoGators/frontend

/apps/algoterminal/                  @AlgoGators/platform
/.github/workflows/app-algoterminal.* @AlgoGators/platform

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Infrastructure and secrets-adjacent config always needs platform review,
# regardless of which service it belongs to. Last match wins, so this is last.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/infra/                             @AlgoGators/platform
**/Dockerfile                       @AlgoGators/platform
**/docker-compose*.yml              @AlgoGators/platform
